WEBVTT

1
00:00:36.986 --> 00:00:40.923
This film is dedicated
to 152 million children

2
00:00:41.091 --> 00:00:43.424
forced into child labor

3
00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:47.424
and all those who fight
for their rights.

4
00:01:21.397 --> 00:01:22.456
We'll be back soon.

5
00:01:22.799 --> 00:01:24.927
- Step on it.
- OK.

6
00:01:29.372 --> 00:01:30.863
That's it. Push it up.

7
00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:32.736
Mamad, take this.

8
00:01:34.077 --> 00:01:35.067
The blocks.

9
00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:39.210
No, I mean the blocks.

10
00:01:39.382 --> 00:01:40.281
All of them.

11
00:02:13.216 --> 00:02:14.479
Unlock it, fast!

12
00:02:20.156 --> 00:02:21.055
Someone is coming.

13
00:02:22.959 --> 00:02:24.427
Hide it under the car.

14
00:02:38.408 --> 00:02:39.774
Abolfazl!

15
00:02:40.476 --> 00:02:41.876
What are you up to?

16
00:02:42.478 --> 00:02:45.004
- What are you doing here?
- I'm lost, sir.

17
00:02:45.215 --> 00:02:46.205
Are you alone?

18
00:02:46.382 --> 00:02:49.750
Lost, really?
Don't panic, I won't hurt you.

19
00:02:50.086 --> 00:02:53.215
If you're lost,
to whom are you sending signals?

20
00:02:54.991 --> 00:02:55.924
Stop!

21
00:02:59.562 --> 00:03:00.791
Get up!

22
00:03:00.964 --> 00:03:01.659
My pants.

23
00:03:02.065 --> 00:03:04.159
Take the tire and the jack!

24
00:03:04.334 --> 00:03:05.996
Go. I'll call you.

25
00:03:07.136 --> 00:03:09.264
- Get your hands off me!
- Let me go!

26
00:03:09.906 --> 00:03:11.204
OK, OK!

27
00:03:12.175 --> 00:03:13.370
Run off, Abolfazl!

28
00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:14.302
Let go of him!

29
00:03:14.711 --> 00:03:18.341
I'll kill you if you come after us.
Got it?

30
00:03:19.048 --> 00:03:19.811
Take this, clown.

31
00:03:19.983 --> 00:03:20.848
Abolfazl, run.

32
00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:24.244
Saeidi!

33
00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:35.262
Run, run!

34
00:03:42.005 --> 00:03:42.995
This way!

35
00:03:48.878 --> 00:03:49.902
Come on.

36
00:04:24.781 --> 00:04:25.840
This way.

37
00:05:25.942 --> 00:05:27.410
Get out of there!

38
00:05:35.418 --> 00:05:42.382
SUN CHILDREN
by Majid Majidi

39
00:05:45.828 --> 00:05:49.128
OTG, USB, chargers...

40
00:05:49.766 --> 00:05:51.291
Need a sponge?

41
00:05:51.467 --> 00:05:53.868
- How much?
- 5,000. You want one?

42
00:05:54.037 --> 00:05:54.834
No.

43
00:05:56.039 --> 00:05:58.304
Sponges, socks...

44
00:05:58.975 --> 00:06:01.410
- Are you going to visit?
- Yes.

45
00:06:02.045 --> 00:06:03.877
Tomorrow we all go to the park.

46
00:06:04.047 --> 00:06:05.379
Wow, lucky!

47
00:06:05.715 --> 00:06:06.375
Are you coming?

48
00:06:06.983 --> 00:06:09.817
No, I am way behind with my studies.

49
00:06:09.986 --> 00:06:12.285
Plus I have to sell all of these.

50
00:06:13.189 --> 00:06:15.090
Who is the new girl?

51
00:06:17.226 --> 00:06:18.353
Which girl?

52
00:06:21.164 --> 00:06:22.097
Messing with me?

53
00:06:22.799 --> 00:06:24.290
Pretty hair clip.

54
00:06:43.719 --> 00:06:46.279
Hi there, 3 packs of cigarettes.

55
00:06:49.459 --> 00:06:51.792
How much for those boxes?

56
00:06:52.195 --> 00:06:53.754
14,000, bro.

57
00:06:54.163 --> 00:06:55.153
Cool, man.

58
00:06:57.733 --> 00:07:00.794
- I beg you.
- You don't get it, she needs rest.

59
00:07:01.204 --> 00:07:03.139
Five minutes and I'm gone.

60
00:07:03.906 --> 00:07:05.101
I'll owe you one.

61
00:07:05.274 --> 00:07:09.370
Take this back, it makes her sick.
Don't bring it again.

62
00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:12.876
I beg you.

63
00:07:13.049 --> 00:07:16.645
You're driving me crazy. Leave.

64
00:07:17.186 --> 00:07:18.415
Go!

65
00:07:18.754 --> 00:07:20.814
Can't handle your kind. Get lost!

66
00:07:20.990 --> 00:07:24.859
You're getting on my nerves.
Not sure I got the pills right!

67
00:07:26.262 --> 00:07:28.788
The visitors are crazier
than the patients!

68
00:08:44.073 --> 00:08:46.736
Reza, over here.

69
00:09:01.324 --> 00:09:03.088
I had something to do.

70
00:09:09.465 --> 00:09:13.402
Promise.
Tomorrow. Morning.

71
00:09:14.036 --> 00:09:15.334
Will tidy up.

72
00:09:36.726 --> 00:09:38.160
- Ali.
- Yes.

73
00:09:38.327 --> 00:09:40.193
- Keshmiri was here.
- What for?

74
00:09:40.363 --> 00:09:43.390
I told him what happened yesterday.
He placed a new order.

75
00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:46.765
One C200 and two BMWs.

76
00:09:47.403 --> 00:09:50.737
- The order and the deposit.
- OK, go back to your work.

77
00:09:56.279 --> 00:09:57.212
Ali,

78
00:09:57.980 --> 00:10:00.040
Rahim is looking for you.

79
00:10:00.249 --> 00:10:01.148
He knows?

80
00:10:01.317 --> 00:10:02.444
What if he finds you here?

81
00:10:02.785 --> 00:10:04.845
Give this to me and tell him I'm out!

82
00:11:15.324 --> 00:11:17.316
Where do you think you're going?

83
00:11:18.494 --> 00:11:20.224
Get on the bike.

84
00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:43.715
- Thanks.
- My pleasure.

85
00:11:43.886 --> 00:11:44.717
Come inside.

86
00:11:47.223 --> 00:11:49.215
What are you doing?

87
00:11:49.392 --> 00:11:50.416
Keep moving!

88
00:11:52.261 --> 00:11:54.196
Quick or you'll see.

89
00:11:56.365 --> 00:11:57.458
Get inside.

90
00:11:59.502 --> 00:12:00.765
This way.

91
00:12:01.337 --> 00:12:02.430
Up the stairs.

92
00:12:03.005 --> 00:12:03.995
Move.

93
00:12:10.846 --> 00:12:11.939
Get in.

94
00:12:14.950 --> 00:12:16.111
Straight on!

95
00:12:20.222 --> 00:12:22.020
Move it!

96
00:12:27.797 --> 00:12:29.026
Here he is, bro.

97
00:12:33.969 --> 00:12:35.267
I regret my mistake, sir.

98
00:12:37.239 --> 00:12:39.799
- When did you catch it?
- I was bringing it back.

99
00:12:40.109 --> 00:12:41.441
I had no idea it was yours.

100
00:12:41.777 --> 00:12:43.473
I realized it yesterday.

101
00:12:43.813 --> 00:12:47.750
It was one of my boys.
He clipped its wings.

102
00:12:48.217 --> 00:12:49.310
Which boys?

103
00:12:50.553 --> 00:12:52.146
The warehouse boys.

104
00:12:52.822 --> 00:12:54.484
They work with me.

105
00:12:56.392 --> 00:12:57.758
How many?

106
00:12:58.527 --> 00:12:59.995
Three, sir.

107
00:13:06.235 --> 00:13:07.203
Sit down.

108
00:13:22.418 --> 00:13:23.408
Eat.

109
00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:29.720
How is your mother?

110
00:13:30.326 --> 00:13:31.885
She's not doing well.

111
00:13:32.228 --> 00:13:34.459
How long will she be staying there?

112
00:13:35.931 --> 00:13:37.695
Until she gets better.

113
00:13:38.367 --> 00:13:40.836
Take her out by all means.

114
00:13:43.439 --> 00:13:46.273
I have no place for her.

115
00:14:03.292 --> 00:14:07.423
What if I provide you with a room?

116
00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:10.966
Can you take care of her?

117
00:14:11.166 --> 00:14:11.997
Yes, sir.

118
00:14:19.174 --> 00:14:20.733
Listen carefully.

119
00:14:21.844 --> 00:14:25.303
Under the cemetery, there is a treasure.

120
00:14:26.515 --> 00:14:28.950
There is no way from the cemetery.

121
00:14:29.151 --> 00:14:33.145
The only way is the school's water pipe
across from it.

122
00:14:35.424 --> 00:14:39.259
We'll do it step by step.
Get it?

123
00:14:39.895 --> 00:14:44.390
First you go to enroll at the school.

124
00:14:44.733 --> 00:14:46.702
Then you'll find the basement.

125
00:14:46.869 --> 00:14:49.896
You keep me posted
and I'll tell you what to do next.

126
00:14:50.940 --> 00:14:51.737
Fine.

127
00:14:52.341 --> 00:14:55.778
Listen, you deal with your boys!

128
00:14:55.945 --> 00:14:58.915
Your responsibility!
I deal with you only.

129
00:14:59.348 --> 00:15:00.941
- Get it?
- Yes, sir.

130
00:15:01.951 --> 00:15:04.682
And you can keep Lady Bird.
She's yours.

131
00:15:04.987 --> 00:15:06.683
Enjoy her.

132
00:15:07.189 --> 00:15:08.418
So nice of you.

133
00:15:10.392 --> 00:15:11.655
With your permission.

134
00:15:21.003 --> 00:15:22.198
That's it!

135
00:15:22.371 --> 00:15:23.464
Treasures!

136
00:15:25.741 --> 00:15:27.369
Of course, you stupid ass.

137
00:15:27.710 --> 00:15:30.145
The deal of a lifetime!

138
00:15:30.746 --> 00:15:32.977
I want a falafel shop.

139
00:15:34.316 --> 00:15:37.184
- Me, a game net shop.
- Keep it down!

140
00:15:38.721 --> 00:15:42.123
Me, a car wash.
Best business ever.

141
00:15:42.291 --> 00:15:45.261
There are a lot of treasures
in my village.

142
00:15:45.427 --> 00:15:48.022
Always protected by a snake.

143
00:15:48.397 --> 00:15:50.366
These are in the basement?

144
00:15:51.333 --> 00:15:51.993
Show us that one.

145
00:15:52.201 --> 00:15:54.227
See, and you didn't believe me.

146
00:15:57.973 --> 00:16:01.842
Wasn't mine. A friend was busy
and asked me to sell it for him.

147
00:16:02.378 --> 00:16:04.279
Ismael knows.

148
00:16:04.446 --> 00:16:06.176
- What do I sell?
- Razors.

149
00:16:06.348 --> 00:16:07.680
You see, Afghan.

150
00:16:08.117 --> 00:16:08.982
Enough!

151
00:16:09.284 --> 00:16:11.719
What did you call him? Afghan?

152
00:16:12.254 --> 00:16:13.847
We're all the same.
Afghans and Iranians.

153
00:16:14.223 --> 00:16:16.192
Back to your class!

154
00:16:19.328 --> 00:16:20.296
Take this.

155
00:16:21.163 --> 00:16:22.756
Maybe you forgot the rest
somewhere else.

156
00:16:22.931 --> 00:16:24.832
- Sir, trust me...
- Just leave.

157
00:16:26.935 --> 00:16:28.460
- Safar?
- Yes?

158
00:16:28.804 --> 00:16:31.672
- Where are the files?
- In a minute.

159
00:16:38.380 --> 00:16:39.211
Stand tall!

160
00:16:42.785 --> 00:16:43.718
You, take off your hat!

161
00:16:46.755 --> 00:16:49.281
- Why did you jump over the wall?
- They didn't let us in.

162
00:16:49.725 --> 00:16:51.250
You jump over the wall
when unwelcome?

163
00:16:55.230 --> 00:16:56.994
We're here to enroll.

164
00:16:58.400 --> 00:17:00.699
- We want to study.
- Now?

165
00:17:01.203 --> 00:17:05.106
Where were you until now?
Come back next year.

166
00:17:05.441 --> 00:17:07.307
Next year is too late.

167
00:17:07.743 --> 00:17:11.976
We've found a part time job,
but we need proof of enrollment.

168
00:17:16.985 --> 00:17:19.887
Fill in the forms
and put down your address.

169
00:17:20.055 --> 00:17:22.991
I'll see if I find another school.

170
00:17:27.129 --> 00:17:27.926
What's this?

171
00:17:28.263 --> 00:17:29.253
To be enrolled here.

172
00:17:29.732 --> 00:17:31.360
It's free to enroll.

173
00:17:32.267 --> 00:17:33.360
Take your money.

174
00:17:34.303 --> 00:17:35.168
I said take it.

175
00:17:37.239 --> 00:17:38.036
Out.

176
00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:40.004
Everyone leaves. You too.

177
00:17:41.143 --> 00:17:43.738
Safar, take them all out.

178
00:17:45.948 --> 00:17:48.110
- Out. Please leave now.
- Let go!

179
00:17:49.017 --> 00:17:51.714
Please, what did we do wrong?

180
00:17:51.887 --> 00:17:53.321
Stop for a sec.

181
00:17:53.489 --> 00:17:56.323
I beg you, sir.
We haven't done anything wrong.

182
00:17:56.492 --> 00:17:57.425
Stop it!

183
00:17:57.760 --> 00:17:59.058
Get out! Out!

184
00:18:02.731 --> 00:18:05.291
Mr. Rafie, come in.

185
00:18:06.735 --> 00:18:10.172
Check the list of kids we recommended
from the past 3 years.

186
00:18:10.339 --> 00:18:12.171
- The brilliant students?
- Yes.

187
00:18:12.341 --> 00:18:13.673
You didn't enroll those boys?

188
00:18:13.976 --> 00:18:16.411
What can I do in this situation?

189
00:18:16.845 --> 00:18:21.112
After 2 weeks only,
they've increased the meal price.

190
00:18:22.451 --> 00:18:24.352
Hello, sir.

191
00:18:24.953 --> 00:18:28.856
You weren't supposed
to increase the prices yet.

192
00:18:33.729 --> 00:18:36.824
It's not 2 or 3 meals but 408!

193
00:18:37.166 --> 00:18:38.964
- Get out.
- You can't force me.

194
00:18:39.802 --> 00:18:43.898
Your small increase
is a big problem for us.

195
00:18:44.873 --> 00:18:47.809
I'll throw you out. You can't fool me.

196
00:18:50.913 --> 00:18:54.350
What's the difference between us?
Aren't we all equals?

197
00:18:57.886 --> 00:18:59.479
We won't leave!

198
00:19:03.725 --> 00:19:04.988
Give me a discount.

199
00:19:05.194 --> 00:19:06.685
Come inside.

200
00:19:07.329 --> 00:19:11.130
You've always been generous
to this school.

201
00:19:37.759 --> 00:19:39.159
What did you write?

202
00:19:39.328 --> 00:19:41.695
We're asked to do addition.

203
00:19:41.864 --> 00:19:44.026
I did the multiplication
and division too.

204
00:19:44.233 --> 00:19:45.895
Great. Continue.

205
00:19:48.470 --> 00:19:49.995
Mohamed Behi?

206
00:19:50.973 --> 00:19:51.770
Yes, sir.

207
00:19:52.341 --> 00:19:53.331
Father's occupation?

208
00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:56.110
He's been absent.

209
00:19:58.247 --> 00:19:59.146
Since when?

210
00:20:00.315 --> 00:20:01.783
As long as I can remember.

211
00:20:02.251 --> 00:20:03.219
Did he ever quit?

212
00:20:04.152 --> 00:20:05.677
Three or four times.

213
00:20:06.889 --> 00:20:10.155
He went to rehab once,
but he started again.

214
00:20:10.959 --> 00:20:12.154
What about you?

215
00:20:12.494 --> 00:20:14.156
My father is in prison.

216
00:20:17.733 --> 00:20:19.793
Mine has been absent too.

217
00:20:20.435 --> 00:20:21.801
What about yours?

218
00:20:22.237 --> 00:20:24.468
I don't have a father. He's dead.

219
00:20:28.977 --> 00:20:30.502
Can I go to the washroom?

220
00:20:32.314 --> 00:20:33.179
Are you done?

221
00:20:34.182 --> 00:20:35.343
As much as I could.

222
00:20:41.990 --> 00:20:45.051
- In total, 37.
- Right. Thank you.

223
00:22:22.057 --> 00:22:26.324
Here, take your SIM card
and your new cell as your prize.

224
00:22:26.895 --> 00:22:29.262
- Use this from now on.
- Cool.

225
00:22:29.431 --> 00:22:35.132
Open the padlock by injecting acid.

226
00:22:35.303 --> 00:22:37.431
- I'll start tomorrow.
- Good boy!

227
00:22:37.773 --> 00:22:40.072
Hey guys! Open the cages!

228
00:22:40.275 --> 00:22:44.736
Let Ali make them fly.

229
00:22:45.847 --> 00:22:46.871
Me?

230
00:22:47.049 --> 00:22:49.746
Absolutely, go on.

231
00:22:49.918 --> 00:22:51.147
So cool.

232
00:23:01.263 --> 00:23:04.700
Feed them well so they come back.

233
00:23:42.737 --> 00:23:44.467
- May I?
- Yes, come in.

234
00:23:46.541 --> 00:23:47.770
Why are you late?

235
00:23:47.943 --> 00:23:49.206
Come to the board!

236
00:23:49.377 --> 00:23:50.401
Back to your seat.

237
00:23:50.745 --> 00:23:53.214
- I'm feeling sick, sir.
- I said to the board!

238
00:23:53.782 --> 00:23:56.718
The greatest source of light is?

239
00:23:56.885 --> 00:23:57.409
The Sun.

240
00:23:57.752 --> 00:23:59.914
Why did you answer? I knew it.

241
00:24:00.088 --> 00:24:02.785
The sun is the greatest source of light.

242
00:24:03.892 --> 00:24:06.361
OK, now answer this question.

243
00:24:08.497 --> 00:24:11.865
Substances in our environment...

244
00:24:12.701 --> 00:24:14.829
How many different states
of the substances are there?

245
00:24:19.341 --> 00:24:20.240
Seven states.

246
00:24:21.376 --> 00:24:23.106
Seven states? Name them?

247
00:24:23.478 --> 00:24:25.276
Heroin, grass, crack...

248
00:24:27.082 --> 00:24:27.947
Shut the hell up!

249
00:24:29.384 --> 00:24:31.751
Ask your mom
to burn you an incense stick!

250
00:24:32.187 --> 00:24:34.122
Quiet. Go back to your seat.

251
00:24:35.023 --> 00:24:38.187
No more washroom during class.

252
00:24:38.360 --> 00:24:42.388
Hence the main source of light
being the sun

253
00:24:42.731 --> 00:24:45.394
how many states of substances are there?

254
00:24:46.067 --> 00:24:47.797
- Three states.
- Name them.

255
00:24:47.969 --> 00:24:49.198
Solid, liquid, gas.

256
00:24:49.371 --> 00:24:50.930
Solid, liquid, gas.

257
00:24:51.273 --> 00:24:53.037
This is not a zoo!

258
00:24:54.976 --> 00:24:56.808
What now?

259
00:24:57.012 --> 00:24:58.275
There was a fight.

260
00:24:59.447 --> 00:25:01.006
Out of here! Out!

261
00:25:07.822 --> 00:25:10.018
Keep your head up!

262
00:25:15.263 --> 00:25:16.094
What's this?

263
00:25:18.133 --> 00:25:20.159
Sorry, but he insulted my mother.

264
00:25:21.937 --> 00:25:23.405
How did you hit them?

265
00:25:25.340 --> 00:25:27.275
Won't do it again!

266
00:25:28.743 --> 00:25:30.974
I'm asking how you fought three
at the same time?

267
00:25:31.313 --> 00:25:33.680
I hit two with my head

268
00:25:33.949 --> 00:25:36.817
and I scared one with the knife.

269
00:25:40.488 --> 00:25:41.751
Get up.

270
00:25:42.524 --> 00:25:43.389
Please forgive me.

271
00:25:43.792 --> 00:25:45.226
I told you to stand up.

272
00:25:45.794 --> 00:25:46.853
Please forgive me.

273
00:25:47.028 --> 00:25:47.893
Stand up.

274
00:25:49.264 --> 00:25:50.232
I'm sorry.

275
00:25:50.398 --> 00:25:51.229
Come closer.

276
00:25:58.306 --> 00:26:00.138
How do you hit with your head?

277
00:26:02.344 --> 00:26:03.835
Raise your hand.

278
00:26:05.347 --> 00:26:06.781
Can I take it?

279
00:26:07.882 --> 00:26:08.850
Take it.

280
00:26:12.420 --> 00:26:17.290
Imagine this is a head and this a nose.

281
00:26:18.226 --> 00:26:20.957
With this part of your head,
you hit his nose.

282
00:26:21.162 --> 00:26:22.221
Which part?

283
00:26:23.198 --> 00:26:26.691
This part, under your hair.

284
00:26:28.737 --> 00:26:30.296
You hit it here.

285
00:26:31.806 --> 00:26:32.466
Hit it.

286
00:26:33.208 --> 00:26:34.437
- Really?
- Yes.

287
00:26:43.051 --> 00:26:44.383
Like this, you'll hurt your nose.

288
00:26:44.719 --> 00:26:46.847
No, you have to practice.

289
00:26:47.455 --> 00:26:50.687
Watch out for your eyebrows.

290
00:26:51.393 --> 00:26:54.488
The way Zeidan
hit his adversary during his last game.

291
00:26:54.929 --> 00:26:57.990
When you hit,
you need to quickly withdraw.

292
00:26:58.466 --> 00:27:02.733
Imagine this is the nose,
you have to hit it with this part.

293
00:27:03.838 --> 00:27:05.136
It wasn't my fault!

294
00:27:05.307 --> 00:27:06.400
Go sit down!

295
00:27:06.741 --> 00:27:09.176
You are all expelled. You too.

296
00:27:09.444 --> 00:27:10.844
You come with me.

297
00:27:11.012 --> 00:27:16.144
- Please forgive me! I'm sorry.
- Hitting your classmates!

298
00:27:16.384 --> 00:27:19.115
Get out! Safar throw them out!

299
00:27:19.287 --> 00:27:20.880
Have pity.
Forgive me, please.

300
00:27:53.221 --> 00:27:55.190
We already agreed on the price.

301
00:27:55.357 --> 00:27:57.485
Careful with the food!

302
00:28:06.901 --> 00:28:08.995
We helped bring the food.

303
00:28:09.804 --> 00:28:11.670
Anything else we could do?

304
00:28:17.946 --> 00:28:21.144
- I give you one week. Just one!
- Thank you, that's great!

305
00:28:21.316 --> 00:28:24.980
Don't leave this here.
Take it to the kitchen. Hurry.

306
00:30:52.534 --> 00:30:53.297
Come here!

307
00:31:01.876 --> 00:31:03.401
Get lost! Go!

308
00:31:03.745 --> 00:31:05.680
- What?
- Mind your business!

309
00:31:06.748 --> 00:31:08.273
Go, you hooligan!

310
00:31:14.389 --> 00:31:15.448
Zahra!

311
00:31:17.859 --> 00:31:18.690
Zahra!

312
00:31:18.860 --> 00:31:22.058
What is it?
That's how you take care of my brother?

313
00:31:22.263 --> 00:31:25.961
You're trying to trick him
with the school enrollment

314
00:31:26.167 --> 00:31:27.863
and the treasure story.

315
00:31:28.036 --> 00:31:30.232
Do you have any idea what you're doing?

316
00:31:30.405 --> 00:31:33.341
Do you know what will happen to us
if the school finds out?

317
00:31:33.508 --> 00:31:38.310
No big deal for you
but for us Afghans it would be terrible!

318
00:31:38.479 --> 00:31:40.380
Do you realize
what will happen to us?

319
00:31:40.548 --> 00:31:44.144
We'll be sent to the refugee camp
and then kicked out of the country!

320
00:31:44.319 --> 00:31:45.719
We'd be miserable.

321
00:31:45.887 --> 00:31:49.915
Listen, let it go or else!

322
00:31:50.091 --> 00:31:53.459
I will come to the school
and tell the director everything.

323
00:31:53.795 --> 00:31:54.888
Got it?

324
00:32:13.214 --> 00:32:16.378
Mom, get up. Let's go!

325
00:32:22.724 --> 00:32:24.693
No way. She can't be released.

326
00:32:24.859 --> 00:32:27.795
Plus she can only be released
by her legal guardian.

327
00:32:27.962 --> 00:32:31.160
It's her aunt
but she's sick and lives far away!

328
00:32:31.532 --> 00:32:32.795
I told you, it's impossible.

329
00:32:32.967 --> 00:32:35.334
If I want to take her home,
who should I talk to?

330
00:32:35.503 --> 00:32:38.029
No idea. You're driving me crazy.

331
00:32:44.312 --> 00:32:45.974
Is this the car accident file?

332
00:32:46.180 --> 00:32:47.944
No, it's the woman
whose house burnt down.

333
00:32:48.116 --> 00:32:50.483
Her daughter died in the fire.

334
00:32:50.818 --> 00:32:52.787
Plus her husband is an addict.

335
00:32:52.954 --> 00:32:56.288
So why do you want
to take your mother home so badly?

336
00:32:56.457 --> 00:32:58.517
Your mother is in really bad shape.
She's in shock.

337
00:32:58.860 --> 00:33:01.989
He makes excuses to have us release her.

338
00:33:02.196 --> 00:33:04.392
Dear boy,
she's not in good condition.

339
00:33:04.732 --> 00:33:07.167
If you want her to recover,
you have to cooperate.

340
00:33:07.869 --> 00:33:10.703
Instead of insisting, think of the day
when she's healthy again

341
00:33:10.872 --> 00:33:12.966
and you can take her
to visit friends and family.

342
00:33:16.411 --> 00:33:17.401
Abolfazl!

343
00:33:17.945 --> 00:33:19.413
I need to speak to you.

344
00:33:23.418 --> 00:33:27.253
Moron! Why the hell
did you tell Zahra about the treasure?

345
00:33:29.023 --> 00:33:31.390
Didn't I tell you
not to tell anyone?

346
00:33:31.926 --> 00:33:33.952
Should I break your jaw?

347
00:33:35.196 --> 00:33:39.759
Tell her we were messing with you.

348
00:33:39.934 --> 00:33:40.958
Got it?

349
00:33:44.172 --> 00:33:45.162
Get lost!

350
00:33:50.945 --> 00:33:52.072
Mamad!

351
00:33:52.880 --> 00:33:53.813
Mamad!

352
00:34:01.255 --> 00:34:03.281
That's Teymour,
the man I told you about.

353
00:34:03.458 --> 00:34:04.426
I'm not going with him!

354
00:34:04.759 --> 00:34:07.422
He's a good man. Go with him to the port.
He'll pay you well.

355
00:34:07.762 --> 00:34:09.424
I don't want this money.

356
00:34:10.398 --> 00:34:11.730
He's an addict.

357
00:34:11.899 --> 00:34:14.232
Stop saying that. Just go.

358
00:34:14.402 --> 00:34:17.338
What's wrong with my job here?

359
00:34:19.507 --> 00:34:20.907
Teymour!

360
00:34:21.075 --> 00:34:24.409
He never lets me keep a job.

361
00:35:03.050 --> 00:35:05.815
Hey bro! We may attract attention!

362
00:35:05.987 --> 00:35:07.979
You go first. I'll catch up later.

363
00:35:27.842 --> 00:35:29.902
So sweet, little chick.

364
00:35:30.077 --> 00:35:32.273
Open it. Let's go in.

365
00:35:37.485 --> 00:35:39.750
My beautiful little chick!

366
00:35:41.255 --> 00:35:42.848
I'll get it for you.

367
00:35:45.092 --> 00:35:47.926
So cute.
Her name could be Goldie?

368
00:35:49.764 --> 00:35:52.233
Get out of there!
The ball isn't in there.

369
00:35:54.101 --> 00:35:56.730
Don't bring her here anymore.
It's dangerous.

370
00:35:56.904 --> 00:35:59.305
There are cats in here.
They might eat her.

371
00:36:02.877 --> 00:36:05.312
Now write down an equivalent fraction.

372
00:36:08.449 --> 00:36:10.145
What about its shape?

373
00:36:18.759 --> 00:36:20.421
Bravo.
Give it up for him.

374
00:36:24.232 --> 00:36:25.427
Where did you learn that Abolfazl?

375
00:36:25.766 --> 00:36:30.466
I worked in construction once.
And this looks like tile work!

376
00:36:30.805 --> 00:36:32.296
You are right.
It does look like tile work.

377
00:36:32.473 --> 00:36:34.874
Give it up for him once more.
Take a seat now.

378
00:36:36.177 --> 00:36:37.042
Your turn.

379
00:36:37.245 --> 00:36:38.941
My town is my home!

380
00:36:39.146 --> 00:36:40.910
Repeat once more.

381
00:36:41.082 --> 00:36:45.884
My town is my home!

382
00:36:46.254 --> 00:36:47.187
Write it down.

383
00:36:47.355 --> 00:36:48.379
Yes, please.

384
00:36:49.257 --> 00:36:53.422
The director wants Abolfazl to pack
his things and come downstairs.

385
00:36:54.095 --> 00:36:55.825
OK! Abolfazl.

386
00:36:55.997 --> 00:36:58.296
Pack your things and go downstairs,
my boy.

387
00:36:58.866 --> 00:37:00.960
Now the second sentence?

388
00:37:01.168 --> 00:37:02.761
- Me!
- Go ahead.

389
00:37:02.937 --> 00:37:04.735
One should not tell lies.

390
00:37:04.906 --> 00:37:07.671
Abolfazl, promise me you won't confess.

391
00:37:07.842 --> 00:37:08.935
Confess what?

392
00:37:09.143 --> 00:37:11.874
Tunnel. Treasure.

393
00:37:13.281 --> 00:37:16.718
Bravo! Show respect to the elderly.

394
00:37:16.884 --> 00:37:20.377
- Repeat the sentence.
- Show respect to the elderly.

395
00:37:21.389 --> 00:37:22.755
Write it down.

396
00:37:25.927 --> 00:37:27.691
- Sir.
- Yes.

397
00:37:27.862 --> 00:37:30.093
May I go to the washroom?
I have stomach ache.

398
00:37:30.264 --> 00:37:32.290
- OK, come back soon.
- OK, sir.

399
00:37:34.869 --> 00:37:36.235
Go see your sister.

400
00:37:38.839 --> 00:37:40.239
You took my notebook!

401
00:37:40.408 --> 00:37:42.877
No, I took mine.

402
00:37:43.044 --> 00:37:47.880
This is yours!
This chicken scratch writing.

403
00:37:48.049 --> 00:37:49.312
Give me your bag!

404
00:37:51.218 --> 00:37:53.210
I'll punish you later!
You'll see!

405
00:37:53.387 --> 00:37:56.323
I've walked a long way for my notebook.

406
00:37:56.490 --> 00:37:59.858
What's this? Tell me.

407
00:38:00.394 --> 00:38:03.990
Take it!
Now I'll be punished because of you!

408
00:38:04.298 --> 00:38:05.322
It's all your fault.

409
00:38:06.033 --> 00:38:06.830
What?

410
00:38:07.001 --> 00:38:09.061
I warned you! You're responsible!

411
00:38:09.236 --> 00:38:11.637
I'll teach you a lesson
when we get home!

412
00:38:14.208 --> 00:38:15.232
What's up?

413
00:38:15.409 --> 00:38:17.674
Nothing!
I took her notebook by mistake.

414
00:38:17.845 --> 00:38:18.972
You ass.

415
00:38:39.133 --> 00:38:40.101
Mamad!

416
00:38:40.267 --> 00:38:41.235
Come here.

417
00:38:49.310 --> 00:38:50.869
See, it's closed.

418
00:38:52.813 --> 00:38:55.180
- What's that?
- I don't know.

419
00:39:56.210 --> 00:39:58.941
Tell him to stop!
They can hear you upstairs!

420
00:39:59.313 --> 00:40:00.178
Ali!

421
00:40:00.781 --> 00:40:02.147
Stop it.
They can hear you!

422
00:40:30.444 --> 00:40:33.004
Such luck!
Now he plays like a champion.

423
00:40:33.214 --> 00:40:34.910
Give me 5,000.

424
00:40:35.416 --> 00:40:37.510
Didn't I tell you
no cigarettes in the school?

425
00:40:40.788 --> 00:40:42.484
- Give me your cigarettes.
- I'll handle it!

426
00:40:42.823 --> 00:40:43.916
Give them to me!

427
00:41:15.990 --> 00:41:16.889
Yes, Maryam.

428
00:41:18.325 --> 00:41:20.487
What the hell were you thinking?

429
00:41:20.828 --> 00:41:23.354
You had no right.
Don't you have a husband?

430
00:41:25.900 --> 00:41:26.868
Hold the line.

431
00:41:28.335 --> 00:41:29.303
Hey you!

432
00:41:31.772 --> 00:41:32.933
What are you doing?

433
00:41:33.240 --> 00:41:34.367
What the hell
are you doing here?

434
00:41:34.542 --> 00:41:36.374
The ball fell down there.

435
00:41:37.111 --> 00:41:39.171
Your ball? Where is it now?

436
00:41:41.815 --> 00:41:44.717
Ali! Come upstairs.
Somebody's here.

437
00:41:46.053 --> 00:41:47.954
- Sir, I messed up.
- Hold on!

438
00:42:02.436 --> 00:42:04.405
Who's there?
Get out of there!

439
00:42:09.043 --> 00:42:09.840
Put it out.

440
00:42:12.513 --> 00:42:13.310
Get out.

441
00:44:13.701 --> 00:44:15.932
Keep going! Don't look back!

442
00:44:16.337 --> 00:44:17.270
OK, OK!

443
00:44:17.905 --> 00:44:19.703
Please let us hide here!

444
00:44:22.276 --> 00:44:26.213
- What if he comes from this door?
- We lost him.

445
00:44:37.091 --> 00:44:38.218
What's the matter?

446
00:44:38.926 --> 00:44:41.259
Quiet! I'm talking!

447
00:44:44.264 --> 00:44:47.029
- What's wrong, Mamad?
- Don't know, man!

448
00:44:47.234 --> 00:44:51.262
This is not legal.
You had no right to lock the door!

449
00:44:51.872 --> 00:44:55.001
You'll be in real trouble
if I file a complaint.

450
00:44:55.209 --> 00:44:58.008
Go for it!
I'm not afraid of your threats!

451
00:44:58.212 --> 00:45:02.980
No rent for eight months.
And three eviction notices!

452
00:45:03.183 --> 00:45:04.674
It's all legal!

453
00:45:04.852 --> 00:45:08.755
Is it legal
to throw these kids in the street?

454
00:45:09.156 --> 00:45:11.819
The law requires you
to respect your contract.

455
00:45:11.992 --> 00:45:15.156
No payment results in eviction.
This is not a crime.

456
00:45:15.729 --> 00:45:19.996
OK, but taking the School of Sun hostage
is a crime.

457
00:45:20.200 --> 00:45:21.133
Open the door!

458
00:45:21.301 --> 00:45:26.365
You were supposed pay the rent
before opening the school.

459
00:45:26.707 --> 00:45:30.371
You know we don't get state subsidies.

460
00:45:30.711 --> 00:45:33.237
We only have private donors.

461
00:45:33.414 --> 00:45:36.043
The school must stay open
to be eligible for financial support.

462
00:45:36.417 --> 00:45:41.355
I'm under pressure too.
The landlord wants his money.

463
00:45:41.522 --> 00:45:45.721
We will pay him.
We just need more time.

464
00:45:45.893 --> 00:45:48.692
When we receive financial aid,
we'll pay you.

465
00:45:48.862 --> 00:45:50.956
Just one week, then kick us out.

466
00:45:51.165 --> 00:45:54.932
I pity the innocent kids
under this incompetent director.

467
00:45:55.269 --> 00:45:56.328
Watch your language!

468
00:45:56.737 --> 00:45:59.138
You ignorant man! How dare you?

469
00:46:06.947 --> 00:46:10.714
I'll show you who's incompetent!

470
00:46:10.884 --> 00:46:12.785
Kids, let's climb the wall!

471
00:47:12.379 --> 00:47:16.942
I am the director of the School of Sun,
a school for street children.

472
00:47:17.150 --> 00:47:18.914
Let me tell you about our school.

473
00:47:19.119 --> 00:47:25.218
We have enrolled 280 exploited children,
exposed to all kinds of social harm.

474
00:47:25.392 --> 00:47:30.353
We try to teach them skills,
how to say no,

475
00:47:30.697 --> 00:47:35.101
and manage their anger
to avoid conflicts and criminal acts.

476
00:47:35.269 --> 00:47:40.173
It wasn't easy
to get them off the streets.

477
00:47:40.340 --> 00:47:42.434
During the past three years,

478
00:47:42.776 --> 00:47:47.111
we've supported 57 brilliant students
to give them a future

479
00:47:47.281 --> 00:47:49.273
either in science or in sports.

480
00:47:49.983 --> 00:47:57.151
Now due to financial problems
we have to close the school.

481
00:47:57.891 --> 00:48:03.762
You have helped us in the past.
We are in dire need of your help again.

482
00:48:04.932 --> 00:48:08.334
We only have one week
to solve our problem.

483
00:48:08.936 --> 00:48:13.306
I ask every one of you to help us.

484
00:48:13.473 --> 00:48:16.272
We are all responsible
for every single child here.

485
00:48:16.443 --> 00:48:18.241
Please help us!

486
00:48:19.980 --> 00:48:21.243
Was it OK?

487
00:48:21.415 --> 00:48:22.405
Perfect.

488
00:48:22.749 --> 00:48:23.682
Let me see it.

489
00:48:25.252 --> 00:48:27.778
OK, right there!
Up there!

490
00:48:31.692 --> 00:48:33.160
Play now!

491
00:48:34.795 --> 00:48:36.024
Do your best.

492
00:48:38.999 --> 00:48:41.025
That's fine.

493
00:48:43.704 --> 00:48:44.967
Come here.

494
00:49:06.727 --> 00:49:08.127
See what's underneath!

495
00:49:10.964 --> 00:49:12.091
That's good.
Bravo!

496
00:49:17.838 --> 00:49:19.397
Are you sure they won't hear you?

497
00:49:19.806 --> 00:49:23.265
No worry, sir.
There is lots of noise upstairs.

498
00:49:47.267 --> 00:49:48.394
Mamad! Pull it!

499
00:49:49.236 --> 00:49:49.999
Shoot!

500
00:49:56.376 --> 00:49:57.776
Move over, Abolfazl.

501
00:50:03.817 --> 00:50:05.115
No, he has never been
in any football club.

502
00:50:08.889 --> 00:50:11.256
Talk to him!

503
00:50:13.527 --> 00:50:16.053
Reza! Reza!
Take this call.

504
00:50:16.263 --> 00:50:17.993
- Hello, sir!
- Hello, how are you?

505
00:50:18.198 --> 00:50:21.396
- What an honor!
- How long have you been playing?

506
00:50:21.968 --> 00:50:23.869
From when I was a small kid, sir.

507
00:50:24.037 --> 00:50:27.439
- Want to join our club?
- It's a dream come true!

508
00:50:27.774 --> 00:50:30.471
OK then.
You'll come see us with Mr. Rafie.

509
00:50:30.811 --> 00:50:32.473
Now let me talk to him.

510
00:50:33.313 --> 00:50:36.750
This boy is really talented.
Bring him to the club.

511
00:50:36.917 --> 00:50:38.715
- Thanks so much!
- I'll be waiting.

512
00:50:50.864 --> 00:50:52.355
Abolfazl, close the door.

513
00:50:57.437 --> 00:50:58.496
Come in!

514
00:51:04.344 --> 00:51:05.368
Reza!

515
00:51:06.379 --> 00:51:08.371
Reza, why did you lock the door?

516
00:51:08.715 --> 00:51:10.445
Ali, I'm leaving.

517
00:51:10.951 --> 00:51:11.975
Where to?

518
00:51:12.185 --> 00:51:16.213
This will change my life.
Do you realize what it means for me?

519
00:51:16.389 --> 00:51:17.755
I'm leaving you, Ali.

520
00:51:17.924 --> 00:51:19.950
I'll kick your ass if you do!

521
00:51:20.427 --> 00:51:21.861
Open the door, I said.

522
00:51:22.028 --> 00:51:24.964
I don't need the treasure.
The club is my treasure.

523
00:51:25.165 --> 00:51:28.192
Soon enough
I'll be joining the National Team.

524
00:51:29.236 --> 00:51:30.864
Abolfazl, open the door.

525
00:51:31.772 --> 00:51:33.331
I said open the door, you ass.

526
00:51:33.507 --> 00:51:34.406
Get lost!

527
00:51:34.741 --> 00:51:37.404
Open the door, Reza,
before anybody shows up.

528
00:51:38.845 --> 00:51:41.940
My mom is so happy about this.

529
00:51:42.315 --> 00:51:45.717
You stupid boy!
There is a treasure down here!

530
00:51:46.186 --> 00:51:51.090
I won't give them a dime.
We'll share it all between us.

531
00:51:51.291 --> 00:51:53.726
Open the door, Reza,
before anybody shows up.

532
00:51:54.261 --> 00:52:00.792
When I get out you'll be dead meat!

533
00:52:04.237 --> 00:52:06.001
You get it, dumbass?

534
00:52:06.206 --> 00:52:08.266
You're always bossing me around!

535
00:52:08.742 --> 00:52:11.177
I don't want to get rich.

536
00:52:11.711 --> 00:52:14.738
You're always threatening to hit me!

537
00:52:15.515 --> 00:52:17.814
Fine, come and hit me!

538
00:52:20.787 --> 00:52:21.914
Come and hit me!

539
00:52:52.853 --> 00:52:53.912
Take a seat.

540
00:52:54.454 --> 00:52:55.752
Hello, Mrs. Rezaie.

541
00:52:58.525 --> 00:52:59.515
Why are you outside?

542
00:52:59.860 --> 00:53:01.692
Why aren't the donors here?
It's getting late.

543
00:53:01.862 --> 00:53:02.761
They will be here soon.

544
00:53:03.363 --> 00:53:05.093
And this is my literature book.

545
00:53:06.733 --> 00:53:11.228
See, finally I ended up in school.
Have a look at the books!

546
00:53:11.771 --> 00:53:12.966
Our school is so cool.

547
00:53:13.306 --> 00:53:17.402
They give us free breakfast and lunch.
We have lots of fun there.

548
00:53:17.744 --> 00:53:20.339
My friends are with me.
We study together.

549
00:53:20.513 --> 00:53:23.677
Abolfazl is in my class.
The other two are next door.

550
00:53:37.530 --> 00:53:38.964
What shall we do?

551
00:53:40.467 --> 00:53:41.691
Mr. Amani?

552
00:53:53.280 --> 00:53:55.214
OK, then we'll start.

553
00:54:24.511 --> 00:54:25.740
Hello.

554
00:54:26.713 --> 00:54:28.306
Welcome.

555
00:54:30.383 --> 00:54:32.284
You made the kids happy.

556
00:54:36.489 --> 00:54:37.980
Kids, you can start.

557
00:56:47.220 --> 00:56:49.045
Abolfazl Shirzad!

558
00:56:51.224 --> 00:56:52.453
Mr. Larijani!

559
00:56:53.226 --> 00:56:57.357
We already introduced
57 brilliant students to you guys.

560
00:56:58.865 --> 00:56:59.764
Yes.

561
00:57:00.433 --> 00:57:02.360
You never gave us a penny.

562
00:57:02.702 --> 00:57:04.330
At least help them now.

563
00:57:05.238 --> 00:57:08.174
Nine of them were Afghans.
He's the tenth!

564
00:57:08.475 --> 00:57:11.912
I sign and stamp it right away.
You'll get the papers right now.

565
00:57:12.312 --> 00:57:16.381
God bless you.
Thank you so much.

566
00:57:18.218 --> 00:57:19.743
Thanks a lot. Bye.

567
00:57:34.267 --> 00:57:39.399
Why is Mr. Ahmadi absent today?
Did he inform you?

568
00:58:00.860 --> 00:58:02.761
I was about to tell you.

569
00:58:04.164 --> 00:58:07.999
Being part of the city council
would make things easier for us.

570
00:58:09.202 --> 00:58:12.001
I can get funding

571
00:58:12.338 --> 00:58:14.807
and use this great opportunity.

572
00:58:15.008 --> 00:58:16.135
For the sake of the kids.

573
00:58:19.145 --> 00:58:20.807
That's what candidates say at first.

574
00:58:21.147 --> 00:58:22.076
Mamad!

575
00:58:25.685 --> 00:58:26.277
Mamad!

576
00:58:30.456 --> 00:58:33.016
Mamad! Your dad is upstairs.
He's starting a fight.

577
00:58:33.226 --> 00:58:34.194
My dad?

578
00:58:37.063 --> 00:58:37.860
Mamad?

579
00:58:38.031 --> 00:58:40.125
What do you think you're doing?

580
00:58:44.971 --> 00:58:45.904
Where are you?

581
00:58:46.072 --> 00:58:47.005
Mamad?

582
00:58:51.911 --> 00:58:52.469
What is it?

583
00:58:52.812 --> 00:58:54.474
Come here.
Come downstairs.

584
00:58:54.814 --> 00:58:56.214
Didn't I tell you
not to show up here?

585
00:58:56.382 --> 00:58:58.010
The man is waiting for you!

586
00:58:58.218 --> 00:59:00.710
To hell with him.
I don't care.

587
00:59:00.887 --> 00:59:02.878
I'll stab you first,
then myself.

588
00:59:03.089 --> 00:59:05.251
He's been waiting for 3 days!

589
00:59:06.693 --> 00:59:08.628
Grab the knife! The knife!

590
00:59:10.263 --> 00:59:11.629
Stay back!

591
00:59:14.934 --> 00:59:16.799
Stop, don't beat him.
He's my dad!

592
00:59:19.272 --> 00:59:21.002
Let me pass!

593
00:59:22.942 --> 00:59:24.069
Move aside!

594
00:59:26.779 --> 00:59:28.077
Make room!

595
00:59:30.283 --> 00:59:31.649
Get back!

596
00:59:35.989 --> 00:59:37.150
Shame on you!

597
00:59:38.491 --> 00:59:39.857
Push back!

598
00:59:40.927 --> 00:59:42.896
Safar! Bring some water.

599
00:59:43.263 --> 00:59:44.697
Some water.

600
00:59:45.999 --> 00:59:47.228
Call an ambulance!

601
00:59:47.400 --> 00:59:50.859
Dad! Don't die on me!
I'll do anything you say!

602
00:59:51.037 --> 00:59:53.939
I'll go anywhere you want!
I swear to God!

603
00:59:54.140 --> 00:59:56.804
Don't worry, Mamad.
It's nothing.

604
00:59:58.811 --> 01:00:01.975
Take him to the room!

605
01:00:56.502 --> 01:00:57.765
Ali!

606
01:01:01.708 --> 01:01:02.932
What's going on?

607
01:01:03.710 --> 01:01:06.202
They arrested Zahra in the subway.

608
01:01:06.379 --> 01:01:07.278
Who?

609
01:01:07.447 --> 01:01:10.975
The municipal Police.
She needs someone to bail her out.

610
01:01:11.951 --> 01:01:14.853
To bail her out? OK.

611
01:01:51.457 --> 01:01:53.756
- Heidari.
- Yes, sir.

612
01:01:53.926 --> 01:01:55.718
You'll be responsible for the kid.

613
01:01:57.997 --> 01:01:59.898
Aren't you being too harsh on them?

614
01:02:00.466 --> 01:02:03.163
You do your job, we do ours.

615
01:02:07.707 --> 01:02:09.833
Go to the end of the corridor.
I'll ask them to bring her.

616
01:02:10.009 --> 01:02:11.204
Thanks a lot.

617
01:02:21.387 --> 01:02:23.217
- Mr. Rafie?
- Yes.

618
01:02:23.389 --> 01:02:25.415
- The discharge papers?
- Here you are.

619
01:02:28.294 --> 01:02:29.455
You may go now.

620
01:03:36.028 --> 01:03:37.462
I'll be back soon.

621
01:03:41.067 --> 01:03:42.898
Did they take your stuff?

622
01:03:56.182 --> 01:03:58.174
- Mr. Ramezani.
- Yes.

623
01:03:58.351 --> 01:03:59.819
What is it?

624
01:04:58.077 --> 01:04:59.409
Thank you.

625
01:05:45.825 --> 01:05:47.259
- Ali.
- Yes, sir.

626
01:05:47.960 --> 01:05:49.895
Abolfazl and his family
plan to go back to Afghanistan.

627
01:05:51.197 --> 01:05:52.426
Going back to Afghanistan?

628
01:05:53.099 --> 01:05:54.294
Too bad.

629
01:05:54.900 --> 01:05:57.495
I wanted to send him to Isfahan
for the math exam.

630
01:05:59.205 --> 01:06:01.140
See if he is making excuses

631
01:06:01.307 --> 01:06:04.800
because this exam
is a great opportunity for his future.

632
01:06:04.977 --> 01:06:05.967
Will do.

633
01:06:49.822 --> 01:06:50.721
Abolfazl!

634
01:06:53.292 --> 01:06:54.351
Abolfazl!

635
01:07:13.946 --> 01:07:15.175
What the hell are you doing here?

636
01:07:15.347 --> 01:07:16.781
My foot got stuck.

637
01:07:16.949 --> 01:07:19.214
Seriously?
What the hell are you up to?

638
01:07:19.852 --> 01:07:21.377
Ali, is the treasure really here?

639
01:07:21.721 --> 01:07:23.451
None of your business.
Get lost!

640
01:07:26.425 --> 01:07:27.654
Wait!

641
01:07:28.394 --> 01:07:29.726
Why didn't you tell me?

642
01:07:29.895 --> 01:07:30.419
What?

643
01:07:30.763 --> 01:07:32.391
That you are going
back to Afghanistan.

644
01:07:33.933 --> 01:07:34.992
I'm talking to you.

645
01:07:35.735 --> 01:07:39.934
Everybody's going back.
My mom said we have to go back too.

646
01:07:41.006 --> 01:07:42.474
All of you?

647
01:07:42.808 --> 01:07:44.140
You have to?

648
01:07:46.912 --> 01:07:49.780
But it's so stupid to leave
when we're almost done.

649
01:07:49.949 --> 01:07:51.440
I'm not the one who decides.

650
01:07:51.951 --> 01:07:53.977
Listen, find a good excuse.

651
01:07:59.959 --> 01:08:02.155
My beautiful chick!

652
01:08:02.328 --> 01:08:05.196
There are cats! Don't go there.

653
01:08:53.312 --> 01:08:54.473
Hi there.

654
01:09:19.705 --> 01:09:20.434
Who opened the door?

655
01:09:21.240 --> 01:09:22.401
Let me explain.

656
01:09:22.741 --> 01:09:23.970
What are you looking for?

657
01:09:24.176 --> 01:09:26.668
- Let me explain.
- I said what are you looking for?

658
01:09:27.680 --> 01:09:28.648
Treasure.

659
01:09:29.882 --> 01:09:30.850
Treasure?

660
01:09:32.117 --> 01:09:33.449
What is he talking about?

661
01:09:33.786 --> 01:09:37.985
There is treasure
at the end of this tunnel.

662
01:09:38.190 --> 01:09:40.216
Underneath the graveyard.

663
01:09:41.227 --> 01:09:42.354
The graveyard?

664
01:09:43.863 --> 01:09:46.458
We're almost there.
Another few meters!

665
01:09:46.799 --> 01:09:48.700
I'm willing to give you a share.

666
01:09:48.868 --> 01:09:51.099
Wait please Mr. Safar!

667
01:09:52.705 --> 01:09:55.231
Wait a second!
For God 's sake.

668
01:09:58.711 --> 01:10:00.737
Please, for God's sake!

669
01:10:08.520 --> 01:10:10.182
Ali, what shall I do now?

670
01:10:10.522 --> 01:10:12.787
You can go. Go!

671
01:10:17.429 --> 01:10:19.295
I know you haven't left wires exposed.

672
01:10:19.465 --> 01:10:21.331
The bulb in the washroom

673
01:10:21.500 --> 01:10:24.766
has blown out 3 times since yesterday.
There could be a short circuit.

674
01:10:25.237 --> 01:10:27.172
The kid was so frightened in there.

675
01:10:28.540 --> 01:10:29.735
Zamani.

676
01:10:33.512 --> 01:10:34.707
No, no.

677
01:10:36.916 --> 01:10:40.876
Classes have already started,
the students are in classrooms.

678
01:10:41.320 --> 01:10:43.186
Let me tell you something.

679
01:10:44.757 --> 01:10:47.317
I think you're used to easy money.

680
01:10:48.861 --> 01:10:51.922
That's exactly it.
Every 2 weeks the same problem.

681
01:10:52.097 --> 01:10:53.725
The school bell is not working.

682
01:10:53.899 --> 01:10:57.461
I have to go around
to announce class is over.

683
01:10:57.803 --> 01:10:58.736
No sir, thank you.

684
01:10:58.904 --> 01:11:02.033
I'll take care of it. Don't bother!

685
01:11:02.241 --> 01:11:05.803
Go and enjoy our money!
Don't need you anymore.

686
01:11:08.814 --> 01:11:10.749
So what shall we do, Ali?

687
01:11:12.184 --> 01:11:14.153
- About?
- Abolfazl.

688
01:11:15.154 --> 01:11:18.056
That's settled.

689
01:11:18.257 --> 01:11:19.384
- Settled?
- Yes, it is.

690
01:11:21.393 --> 01:11:22.884
You need to talk to me?

691
01:11:25.197 --> 01:11:26.722
No, would you like more tea?

692
01:11:27.099 --> 01:11:28.328
No, thanks.

693
01:11:32.204 --> 01:11:35.140
Your ID was left with me.

694
01:11:35.808 --> 01:11:37.174
It's very kind of you, sir.

695
01:11:40.446 --> 01:11:41.846
Mr. Safar.

696
01:11:43.282 --> 01:11:44.910
For God 's sake.

697
01:11:46.051 --> 01:11:47.713
You'll get your share.

698
01:11:48.420 --> 01:11:49.718
Thanks for not telling him.

699
01:11:49.888 --> 01:11:52.255
I swear on my mom's life,
you'll get your share.

700
01:11:53.359 --> 01:11:55.328
What are you doing, Mr. Safar?

701
01:11:55.761 --> 01:11:56.751
Mr. Safar!

702
01:11:58.530 --> 01:12:00.465
For the sake of your child, please!

703
01:12:20.085 --> 01:12:21.109
Coming.

704
01:12:22.988 --> 01:12:23.956
Who's there?

705
01:12:24.356 --> 01:12:27.155
It's me, Ali Zamani.
I'm one of the students.

706
01:12:27.326 --> 01:12:28.487
What do you want?

707
01:12:29.862 --> 01:12:32.195
Would you open the door.
I'm here to see Mr. Safar.

708
01:12:32.364 --> 01:12:35.425
- He's not in. He's outside.
- He's not in?

709
01:12:36.268 --> 01:12:38.737
- When did he leave?
- Hours ago.

710
01:12:40.272 --> 01:12:42.741
Let him know that I'll be waiting.

711
01:12:42.908 --> 01:12:46.345
Don't waste your time.
Not sure when he'll be back.

712
01:12:59.558 --> 01:13:02.357
Sweetie, play here.
I'll be back soon.

713
01:13:49.541 --> 01:13:50.702
Come on in.

714
01:14:18.837 --> 01:14:23.969
So the perimeter of a square
is one side's length multiplied by 4.

715
01:14:24.176 --> 01:14:29.114
What about the perimeter of a rectangle?

716
01:14:31.150 --> 01:14:32.778
Anybody?

717
01:15:50.395 --> 01:15:51.488
Yes, please!

718
01:15:51.830 --> 01:15:52.763
- Teacher?
- Yes?

719
01:15:52.931 --> 01:15:54.490
School bell is not working.
It's breaktime.

720
01:15:54.833 --> 01:15:58.031
To be continued later.
Don't push each other.

721
01:15:58.971 --> 01:16:00.872
Careful, guys.

722
01:16:02.007 --> 01:16:04.238
Get up Ali, it's breaktime.

723
01:16:09.848 --> 01:16:12.181
Break time.
The bell is out of order.

724
01:16:13.485 --> 01:16:15.010
- Zamani.
- Sir?

725
01:16:15.420 --> 01:16:18.083
Go to the office and ring the bell.
Let's see if it's working.

726
01:16:18.457 --> 01:16:19.652
Sure, sir.

727
01:16:26.798 --> 01:16:27.731
Did you do it?

728
01:16:28.967 --> 01:16:30.936
Yes, the switch is on.

729
01:16:33.005 --> 01:16:35.804
- Leave it on.
- Yes, sir.

730
01:16:42.414 --> 01:16:44.042
Should be that yellow wire.

731
01:16:44.249 --> 01:16:45.842
No dear!
The black wire is the one.

732
01:16:46.218 --> 01:16:48.847
No sir, I am sure it's the yellow one.

733
01:16:49.021 --> 01:16:50.045
You should check it
with the phase meter.

734
01:16:50.722 --> 01:16:52.884
It's not working either.
But I'm sure that's the one.

735
01:16:53.225 --> 01:16:54.215
Shall we bet?

736
01:16:55.761 --> 01:16:56.854
The winner gets a smoothie.

737
01:16:57.029 --> 01:16:58.497
Sure, let's bet on it.

738
01:16:59.998 --> 01:17:00.693
Mr. Rafie.

739
01:17:01.900 --> 01:17:03.266
The police are here.

740
01:17:03.468 --> 01:17:05.699
- Here, in the school?
- Yes, they are coming inside.

741
01:17:08.674 --> 01:17:10.165
Officer,
here's the coward I told you about.

742
01:17:10.809 --> 01:17:13.176
We summoned you yesterday,
but you didn't show up.

743
01:17:13.345 --> 01:17:14.745
You have to come with us.

744
01:17:14.913 --> 01:17:16.347
- What's wrong officer?
- There is a complaint.

745
01:17:16.682 --> 01:17:17.411
Nothing major.

746
01:17:17.749 --> 01:17:20.241
Nothing major? You broke my nose.

747
01:17:20.419 --> 01:17:23.150
You can't do whatever you want.
I'll teach you a lesson.

748
01:17:24.823 --> 01:17:25.722
Ali, stop it.

749
01:17:26.758 --> 01:17:28.818
- Ali, behave yourself.
- He insulted you.

750
01:17:28.994 --> 01:17:30.986
Where are they taking you?

751
01:17:31.196 --> 01:17:32.255
It's all his fault.

752
01:17:32.431 --> 01:17:33.126
Stay back.

753
01:17:33.298 --> 01:17:33.958
Mr. Rafie.

754
01:17:34.900 --> 01:17:37.028
Where are you taking him, officer?

755
01:17:47.779 --> 01:17:49.372
Call Amani!

756
01:17:53.518 --> 01:17:55.282
You should be ashamed of yourselves.

757
01:17:55.921 --> 01:17:58.254
- Who was that?
- Ali, sir.

758
01:18:03.261 --> 01:18:05.321
Hands off. Stay back.

759
01:18:10.969 --> 01:18:12.835
Mr. Rafie,
I'm coming to the police station.

760
01:18:13.872 --> 01:18:14.840
Stay back.

761
01:20:16.761 --> 01:20:20.425
- Are you sure you threw it in there?
- I threw it and I ran.

762
01:20:34.045 --> 01:20:35.809
- What's that?
- What?

763
01:20:38.116 --> 01:20:39.015
This.

764
01:20:43.288 --> 01:20:44.916
How come we missed this?

765
01:20:50.028 --> 01:20:52.998
I tripped and fell down.

766
01:20:53.198 --> 01:20:54.962
Might be this one then.

767
01:20:55.133 --> 01:20:56.999
Yes, I'm sure this is the right one.

768
01:20:57.202 --> 01:21:03.199
This is another water pipe.
He has to take down the wall in between.

769
01:21:04.075 --> 01:21:05.668
Damn, what to say to the boy?

770
01:21:05.844 --> 01:21:08.973
You make a fuss.
I'll handle him.

771
01:21:10.715 --> 01:21:13.378
Told you not to trust that kid.
He's a loser.

772
01:21:14.319 --> 01:21:16.151
You didn't listen to me

773
01:21:16.321 --> 01:21:18.017
and trusted him.

774
01:21:18.223 --> 01:21:19.919
He will ruin the whole plan
and get us into trouble.

775
01:21:20.091 --> 01:21:21.923
This is not his fault.

776
01:21:22.327 --> 01:21:24.455
On the contrary, he's very capable.

777
01:21:26.398 --> 01:21:31.063
Listen!
We were told to dig both sides.

778
01:21:31.736 --> 01:21:34.729
If not in one pipe, then in the other.

779
01:21:35.240 --> 01:21:37.266
Did you say the opposite path is closed?

780
01:21:37.442 --> 01:21:38.410
Yes.

781
01:21:39.544 --> 01:21:41.479
But don't worry, I'll open it fast.

782
01:21:42.080 --> 01:21:44.379
Bravo, go for it.

783
01:21:44.549 --> 01:21:49.920
And call me as soon as you get
on the other side.

784
01:21:51.222 --> 01:21:52.155
OK, sir.

785
01:21:52.324 --> 01:21:54.316
Show me what you're made of.

786
01:23:24.883 --> 01:23:26.476
Keep moving.

787
01:33:58.316 --> 01:34:02.378
SUN CHILDREN

788
01:34:08.225 --> 01:34:11.821
Directed by
Majid Majidi

789
